Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-03-2000||10:21 PM||||I'm a proud owner of a 1985 Pontiac Fiero GT. V6 with a automatic transmission.  BEAUTIFUL, body needs a little works and a spoiler, and the interior need new seat and center console.  I don't care how ugly it is it's beautiful  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Ok, here's the thing, the computer shorted out and caught on fire, not much damage... it need a new computer and the harness wire from the computer to the firewall.  it's a bi*ch to find a computer for those (around here in ohio)... can I take a computer that's from 86 fiero se with v6 and auto tranny and put it in my Fiero?  Thanks for any responds  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-03-2000||10:25 PM||||There shouldn't be any different between the 85-86 computers.  Somebody stop me if I'm wrong! Just remember if you take the computer from a manual transmission car, you need the PROM(chip) from YOUR computer or another automatic.   The computer is the same, but the chip is not.||||reg||3
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||04-03-2000||11:28 PM||||I am almost positive there is a differance between 85 and later V6 computers. I think there are more differances between the 85 and the 86-87's than there is between the 88 and 86-87's. Not exactly sure what though.||||reg||1
